<title>SOUTH KOREA: Strikes cost S.Korea over $3 billion in lost output.</title>
<headline>Strikes cost S.Korea over $3 billion in lost output.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea is expected to post 2.68 trillion won ($3.15 billion) in lost production because of more than three weeks of wildcat strikes, a trade ministry official said.</p>
<p>Lost exports from the start of industrial action on December 26 were estimated to be $483 million, he said.  </p>
<p>South Korea's major industries were disrupted by protests at the passage of a new labour law, which allows employers to lay off workers, replace strikers and implement flexible work hours.</p>
<p>Factories resumed production on Monday after the militant Korean Confederation of Trade Unions called off indefinite strikes and limited stoppages to once a week on Wednesdays.</p>
